    ["compressed_files",
    ".PF",
    "Private File",
    "4.0",
    "A PF file is a password-protected file compressed and encrypted by Stuffit Deluxe, a popular file compression and expansion utility. It is similar to a.SIT file, but requires a password to decrypt and decompress. PF files are often used for archiving confidential or personal data. You can open PF files with Stuffit Deluxe in Windows or macOS. However, the PF files will not open unless the correct password is entered. Also, it is important to extract the contents of a PF file on a safe device because the contents, which may be documents, images, videos, etc., are most likely sensitive. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. A PF file is a log file used by Prefetcher, a Windows Memory Manager component that speeds up the boot process and application launches. It contains a record of data access events recorded during the boot process or an application launch. PF files allow Windows to more efficiently access and load resources when you start Windows or open a program. Microsoft introduced the Prefetcher in Windows XP. The Prefetcher records what data is accessed when the system boots or an application launches. It then saves a record of these data access events in a PF file. When you start Windows or open an application for which a PF file exists, Windows uses the related PF file to more quickly load the data needed to complete that process. Each PF file is named for the process or application with which it is used. For example, the PF file used as part of the system boot process is always named NTOSBOOT-B00DFAAD.PF; the PF file used when launching Mozilla Firefox is named FIREFOX.EXE-25FC0A66.PF. All PF files are stored in Windows C:/​Windows/​Prefetch directory. This directory may also contain other Prefetch-related files. PF files are not meant to be opened. Windows Microsoft Prefetcher.",
    "Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Windows Microsoft Prefetcher.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".DZ",
    "Dzip File",
    "4.0",
    "Compressed file created by Dzip, a command line utility used for compressing and decompressing files; saves the archive in a proprietary format that sometimes can be created and extracted more quickly and with a higher compression ratio than other compression methods. Because of its small file size, the Dzip program is sometimes saved to discs alongside the compressed DZ files. Windows Dzip. Mac Dzip. Linux DzipFree. Game file used by Land of the Dead: Road to Fiddlers Green, a zombie first-person shooter game; saves the structure of a level and includes terrain, buildings, items, and other map features; stored in the /​Land of the Dead/​Levels/​ directory. Windows BrainBox Games Land of the Dead Unreal Tournament Package ToolFree.",
    "Windows Dzip. Mac Dzip. Linux Dzip. Windows BrainBox Games Land of the Dead Unreal Tournament Package Tool.",
    "?"],
