    ["compressed_files",
    ".TX_",
    "Compressed Text File",
    "3.8",
    "A TX_ file is a compressed.TXT file typically created by Makecab, a Windows utility used for compressing files and generating.CAB files. It is often used for saving a TXT file to a CD so that it uses less disc space. To decompress a TX_ file in Windows with Microsoft Expand installed, type the following command: expand myfile.tx_ myfile.txt NOTE: The underscore syntax is also used for many other compressed file types, including.EX_,.DL_, and.SY_. Windows Microsoft Expand —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS.",
    "Windows Microsoft Expand —  (Discontinued)  Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".PAR2",
    "Parchive 2 File",
    "3.8",
    "A PAR2 file is a parity volume or index created by Parchive 2 (PAR2). PAR2 parity volumes are used to recover a damaged or missing file included in a group of files. PAR2 indexes are used to identify and verify the integrity of files associated with a set of parity volumes. Parchive is a program that allows users to create parity volumes associated with a group of files. Using the parity volumes, users can restore any files that go missing from the group or become damaged. For example, if a user shares a set of files online, and one of the files becomes corrupted, other users can use the parity volumes associated with that group of files to restore the corrupted file. The second version of Parchive, known as Parchive 2 or PAR2, saves parity volumes as PAR2 files. It also saves a small index file, used to identify and verify the integrity of associated files, with the.par2 extension. You can open a PAR2 file with QuickPar (Windows), MultiPar (Windows), MacPAR deluxe (Mac), or PyPar2 (Linux). Windows QuickPar. MultiPar. Mac MacPAR Deluxe. Linux PyPar2Free.",
    "Windows QuickPar. MultiPar. Mac MacPAR Deluxe. Linux PyPar2.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".ARI",
    "ARI Compressed Archive",
    "3.8",
    "An ARI file is a still frame image recorded by an ARRI digital video camera, such as ALEXA MINI and AMIRA. It stores uncompressed image data in the ARRIRAW format exactly how the sensor on the camera captured it. ARI files are single still frames from a sequence of images that comprise a recorded video. ARI file open in ARRIRAW Converter 4.3 ARRI Group is a German camera manufacturer specializing in producing motion picture cameras and lenses. Professional video editors and cinematographers often work with ARRI cameras and.MXF video files. However, video editors may work with individual ARI still frame files that make up the more extended video sequence to modify its properties more accurately. For example, they may alter the coloring of the still frame or apply special effects. You can open an ARI file with several applications. ARRIRAW Converter can view ARI files and convert them to other formats. You can also open ARI files with Microsoft Photos (with the RAW Image extension) and various third-party applications with the ARRI SDK. Windows File Viewer Plus. ARRIRAW Converter. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe SpeedGrade —  (Discontinued). Mac ARRIRAW Converter. Apple Final Cut Pro with Glue Tools Cineon/DPX Pro plugin. Adobe SpeedGrade —  (Discontinued). Linux ARRIRAW Converter. Android File Viewer for Android. An ARI file is a compressed archive created by ARI, an archive utility for DOS. It contains one or more compressed files. Compressing files into an ARI file allows users to store and share those files more efficiently. ARI was an archiving utility developed by RAO. It was available in both free and paid versions, with the paid version including extra features. The utility compressed files using arithmetic coding, producing ARI archives. ARI users could combine this compression method with other compression algorithms, including LZP, DC, BWT, and PPM, to further compress their files. You can open an ARI file with ARI. Because ARI is available only for DOS, you may have to run it in an MS-DOS emulator, such as DOSbox. Windows RAO ARIFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. ARRIRAW Converter. Microsoft Photos Included with OS. Adobe SpeedGrade —  (Discontinued). Mac ARRIRAW Converter. Apple Final Cut Pro with Glue Tools Cineon/DPX Pro plugin. Adobe SpeedGrade —  (Discontinued). Linux ARRIRAW Converter. Android File Viewer for Android. Windows RAO ARI.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".CZIP",
    "ZipGenius CryptoZip File",
    "3.8",
    "A CZIP file is an archive encrypted in the proprietary CryptoZip (CZIP) format by ZipGenius, a free archive manager for Windows. It stores one or more Zip-compressed files encrypted with the CZIP, Blowfish 128-bit, Twofish, or Rijndael 128-bit methods and may be password-protected. ZipGenius users compress archives as CZIP files to share data with others securely. CZIP file open in ZipGenius 6 The ZipGenius Team (formerly WinInizio Software) develops ZipGenius. The Zip utility supports compressing and extracting various archive formats, including.ZIP,.CBZ,.TAR.GZ,.7Z, and.LZH. The CZIP format supports various options for compressing archives, including Standard, Self-locking, and Self-erasing types. Furthermore, you can only extract self-locking and self-erasing archives with the correct passphrase (three incorrect passwords renders the file unrecoverable). You can also add your name or email address and choose the archive version when compressing the CZIP archive. How to create a CZIP file with ZipGenius To create a CZIP file, select Tools → Encrypt / decrypt archive. Depending on your chosen encryption method, you will encounter different prompts to create the CZIP file. For example, if you choose the Twofish method, you must enter a passphrase for securing the CZIP archive before creating it. You can open a CZIP file with ZipGenius in Windows. To open a CZIP file, select File → Open. Windows ZipGeniusFree.",
    "Windows ZipGenius.",
    "ZipGenius can extract files from CZIP archives, then compress them in other formats, including the following types:.ZIP - Zipped File.7Z - 7-Zip Compressed File.TAR - Consolidated Unix File Archive.CAB - Windows Cabinet File.CBZ - Comic Book Zip Archive.LZH - LZH Compressed File."],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".LZ4",
    "LZ4 Compressed File",
    "3.8",
    "An LZ4 file is a compressed archive created by one of a variety of LZ4 compression utilities, most notably the lz4 command-line utility. It contains one or more files that have been compressed using LZ4 compression. LZ4 files can be decompressed using the lz4 command-line utility and other LZ4 utilities. In 2011, Yann Collet released the initial version of the LZ4 data compression algorithm. Based on the LZ77 compression algorithm, LZ4 is a notably fast compression system, allowing users to compress and decompress files quickly. Over time, other contributors have helped refine the LZ4 compression algorithm, and the algorithms use has increased. For example, Linux systems now natively support LZ4 compression and decompression, allowing users to create and extract files from LZ4 archives using lz4 and other, related command-line commands. You can extract the files contained within an LZ4 archive using the lz4 command-line utility (cross-platform) or a variety of other LZ4 decompression utilities. All these utilities can be downloaded from LZ4s website (lz4.github.io/lz4). Windows LZ4. Mac LZ4. Linux LZ4Free.",
    "Windows LZ4. Mac LZ4. Linux LZ4.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".ZIX",
    "WinZix Compressed File",
    "3.8",
    "File archive compressed using WinZix compression; claims to use a higher compression ratio and perform faster compression than comparable file archiving utilities. NOTE: WinZix has been known to install spyware on computers and may not compress files. Therefore, using WinZix is not recommended. Windows WinZix UnZix UnZixWin Linux WinZix Console version. A ZIX file is a data file used by older versions of Intuit Quicken, a financial management app. It stores financial data entered by a user, such as their transactions and investments. Quicken no longer stores data in ZIX files. Intuit Quicken is an application for Windows and macOS that helps you manage your finances and investments. The software allows you to track transactions, create budgets, and organize assets. Earlier versions of Quicken used ZIX, ZDB, and CHG files to store financial data that the software referenced when loading information in the app. However, Quicken no longer uses ZIX files, making them rare. ZIX files are not meant to be manually opened. Instead, Intuit Quicken references the data stored in the ZIX file. However, Quicken no longer supports ZIX files. Windows Intuit Quicken. Mac Intuit Quicken.",
    "Windows WinZix UnZix UnZixWin. Linux WinZix Console version. Windows Intuit Quicken. Mac Intuit Quicken.",
    "?"],
