    ["compressed_files",
    ".PIZ",
    "Zipped File",
    "3.6",
    "A PIZ file is a compressed.ZIP archive that has been renamed with the extension reversed. It contains one or more files that have been compressed with Zip compression. PIZ files are often used for hiding the file type when sending zipped email attachments so that email server filters dont block the message. If you receive a PIZ file you should verify the identity of the sender in order to ensure that the file does not contain malware. Once you verify that the file is safe, rename the .piz extension to .zip and open it with any Zip decompression utility. Some popular programs are WinZip, Win RAR, 7-Zip, and Stuffit Deluxe. Windows Corel WinZip. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. 7-Zip. RARLAB WinRAR. Mac Corel WinZip Mac. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS.",
    "Windows Corel WinZip. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. 7-Zip. RARLAB WinRAR. Mac Corel WinZip Mac. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".Z00",
    "Split Zip Archive",
    "3.6",
    "A Z00 file is a split archive that contains one or more files that have been compressed with Zip compression to save space. It is one of multiple files (.Z01,.Z02, etc.) that make up a complete archive. Z00 split archives may be created by various compression utilities to shrink the size of large files for transfer or archival purposes. Split archives are especially useful when transferring files via e-mail attachments because emails have significant file size limitations. However, with the advancement of Internet speeds and cloud storage capabilities, split archives are not as common or necessary as they once were. Users can upload their files to a cloud storage space, such as Google Drive or Dropbox more easily and share a link with the recipient who can then download the files. You can open a Z00 split archive with various compression utilities, such as 7-Zip (Windows), Corel WinZip (Windows), or Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac (macOS). Keep in mind that a Z00 file can only be decompressed if the related split archives (Z01, Z02, etc.) are available. Windows Corel WinZip. RARLAB WinRAR. 7-Zip. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The UnarchiverFree.",
    "Windows Corel WinZip. RARLAB WinRAR. 7-Zip. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The Unarchiver.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SPA",
    "Spotify Application",
    "3.6",
    "3D model effects file used by MikuMikuDance, a dance and rhythm synchronization game; saved as a.BMP image but uses the .spa extension instead; used for adding a shiny look to 3D model features such as hair or clothes. SPA files may also incorporate transparency (e.g.,.PNG or.TGA files), but they are most commonly created from non-transparent bitmap images. NOTE: You can create a SPA file by drawing a Bitmap image (.bmp file) with any graphics editor and renaming the extension to .spa.. Windows MikuMikuDanceFree. A SPA file is a Zip-compressed application used by the Spotify desktop app. It contains component files, including.CSS,.HTML,.JSON, and.JS files, used to load and display a feature (such as Browse, About, or Follow) in Spotify. SPA files are found in Spotifys Apps folder. Spotify is an audio streaming service that allows listeners to search for and play any of over 60 million songs and podcasts. Listeners can also create their own Spotify playlists and share them with others or rely on Spotifys recommendations to play a radio-like stream of songs. While most people listen to Spotify via the services mobile apps, Spotify also offers a desktop application that Mac and Windows users can download and use to listen to audio on their PCs. To show features to listeners, the Spotify desktop app references a series of SPA files that are saved in the apps Apps folder. For example, if you navigate to Spotifys Apps folder, youll see a file named browse.spa. When you click the Spotify desktop apps Browse button, Spotify accesses browse.spa and uses it to load the Browse feature. (You can also access the Browse feature by searching for spotify:browse in Spotifys search bar, which causes the app to access browse.spa.) Each SPA file is a Zip-compressed file that contains a series of other files. These component files are used to properly load and display each SPA files associated feature. For example, if you rename about.spa to about.zip, decompress it, and open the about folder that appears, youll find the set of files used to show the Spotify desktop apps About Spotify window. Spotify SPA files are not meant to be opened. However, if you want to view the files contained within a SPA file, you can rename the file to use the.ZIP extension, decompress it, and view its contents as you would any Zip archive. Also, you can open some SPA files in Spotify by searching for spotify:filename in the Spotify desktop apps search bar. For example, you can open the About Spotify window by searching for spotify:about, and you can open the Browse feature by searching for spotify:browse. Windows Spotify. 7-Zip. Mac Spotify. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. An SPA file is a spectrum analysis produced using an Anritsu Spectrum Analyzer. It contains a trace of a signals amplitude and frequency. You can open SPA files in Anritsu Master Software Tools. Anritsu is a Japanese electronics equipment manufacturer that produces, among many other items, spectrum analyzers. Spectrum analyzers are used primarily to measure a signals amplitude and frequency, to see if the signals measurements remain within required limits. There are many different types of spectrum analyzers, some of which measure additional types of data. Many of Anritsus spectrum analyzers save measurements as SPA files. Users can transfer SPA files to their computer to view the measurements the files contain in Anritsu analysis programs, such as Master Software Tools. You can open an SPA file in Anritsu Master Software Tools (Windows). Master Software Tools is a free program that comes included with Anritsus Software Tool Box. Windows Anritsu Master Software ToolsFree. Particle file used by Nintendo DS games, such as New Super Mario Bros. and Mario Kart; contains images used to illustrate particles, such as sand, dust, and sparks, for animations. The SPA file is referenced by the game to illustrate splashing water, fire explosions, and other game actions. The file can also be edited to modify the appearance of the particles. Windows MKDS Course ModifierFree.",
    "Windows MikuMikuDance. Windows Spotify. 7-Zip. Mac Spotify. Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. Windows Anritsu Master Software Tools. Windows MKDS Course Modifier.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SIFZ",
    "Synfig Studio Compressed Project",
    "3.6",
    "A SIFZ file is a.SIF project compressed with gzip and created by Synfig Studio, an open source application used to create professional 2D animations. It contains an animation, which consists of a canvas filled with shapes, brush or pencil strokes, text, and position, radius, tangent, angle, vertex, and width handles. SIFZ files are one of three file formats used by Synfig Studio but are also the most common format used. Since they compress their contents they are smaller in size than uncompressed SIF files that often become bloated. Synfig Studio also uses.SFG files for embedding images, audio, etc. into the project which is compressed with Zip compression. Mac Synfig Studio. Windows Synfig Studio. Linux Synfig StudioFree.",
    "Mac Synfig Studio. Windows Synfig Studio. Linux Synfig Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SITX",
    "StuffIt X Archive",
    "3.6",
    "A SITX file is a compressed file saved in the Stuffit X archive format, the default format used by StuffIt 7.0 and later. It features Smith Micros exclusive ATOM compression technology and offers up to 20% more compression than standard Stuffit (.SIT) archives. The SITX format supports long filenames, preservation of UNIX (i.e. OS X) and Windows file permissions, and error correction, which fixes data transmission errors. It also supports password protection using 512-bit RC4 encryption or other encryption methods, including AES, DES, and Blowfish. Version 9 and later provides 15-30% compression of JPEG images. NOTE: StuffIt was previously developed by Allume Systems (formerly Aladdin Systems), but is now developed and distributed by Smith Micro. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Smith Micro StuffIt Expander. Incredible Bee Archiver. The Unarchiver. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Smith Micro StuffIt Expander. iOS Smith Micro StuffIt ExpanderFree.",
    "Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Smith Micro StuffIt Expander. Incredible Bee Archiver. The Unarchiver. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Smith Micro StuffIt Expander. iOS Smith Micro StuffIt Expander.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".PEA",
    "PEA File Archive",
    "3.6",
    "Compressed file archive created with PeaZip, an file archiving, encryption, and file splitting tool; supports deflate-based compression, multi-volume file spanning, AES256 in EAX mode for authenticated encryption; also uses a cryptographically strong hash to check file and volume integrity. PEA stands for Pack, Encrypt, Authenticate and is a security-focused archive format. Windows PeaZip. Linux PeaZipFree.",
    "Windows PeaZip. Linux PeaZip.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".LZ",
    "Lzip Compressed File",
    "3.6",
    "File archive compressed with Lzip, a lossless data compressor based on the LZMA (Lempel-Ziv-Markov chain) algorithm; supports higher compression ratios than bzip2 and includes a 32-bit CRC checksum for checking the integrity of the file. Windows Lzip. Mac Lzip. Keka. Linux LzipFree.",
    "Windows Lzip. Mac Lzip. Keka. Linux Lzip.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".CBA",
    "Comic Book ACE Archive",
    "3.6",
    "Digital comic book compressed with ACE compression (.ACE files); contains a collection of images that represent pages in the comic book; used for distributing comic books and reading them with supporting e-readers. The CBA format is much less common than the.CBR,.CBZ, and.CB7 formats, which use more popular forms of compression (.RAR,.ZIP, and.7Z). Windows CDisplayExFree. File used by the CryENGINE SDK, a collection of applications used for developing games for the PC and console platforms; saves settings for compiling 3D model skeletons into the.DBA format, which is used by the video game. CBA files are specified in an XML format and include references to character models (.CHR) and the output database assets (DBA) file. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "Windows CDisplayEx. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".WAR",
    "Java Web Archive",
    "3.6",
    "A WAR file is a compressed package containing Java-based web components and applications that are run on a web server. It is formatted the same way as a.JAR file, but includes additional information that tells the application server which Java servlet class to run. WAR files may contain server-side utility classes (such as database beans and shopping carts), static web resources (HTML, image, and sound files), and client-side classes (applets and utility classes). They can be run on a web server using a supporting program such as the Tomcat Web Application Manager within Apache. Since WAR files are saved in an archive format, the contents of a WAR file can be extracted using a file decompression utility like Stuffit Expander. Windows File Viewer Plus. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. RARLAB WinRAR. ESTsoft ALZip. Apache Tomcat. Mac Corel WinZip Mac. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Apache Tomcat. Linux Apache Tomcat. unrar.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. RARLAB WinRAR. ESTsoft ALZip. Apache Tomcat. Mac Corel WinZip Mac. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Apache Tomcat. Linux Apache Tomcat. unrar.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".FDP",
    "MySafe Encrypted Data",
    "3.6",
    "Encrypted file or folder used to protect important files; only accessible using fingerprint reader authentication. Windows UPEK Protector Suite QL. Project file created by FMOD, a sound design tool used for authoring game sounds; saves the design for audio events, which are sounds (i.e., footsteps, explosions, and ambient sounds) that can be invoked in the games program code; allows the sounds to be programmatically triggered and customized while the game is running, which creates a more immersive gameplay environment. An FMOD project is built into an FMOD Events (.FEV) file and an FMOD Sound Bank (.FSB) file. These two files are used by the game runtime to trigger and play audio events. NOTE: FDP files were replaced by FSPRO files when FMOD Designer was renamed FMOD Studio. However, FDP files can still be opened by FMOD Studio. Windows Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio. Mac Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio.",
    "Windows UPEK Protector Suite QL. Windows Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio. Mac Firelight Technologies FMOD Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SDC",
    "Secure Download Cabinet",
    "3.5",
    "Compressed and encrypted archive used for installing MSDNAA (Microsoft Developer Network Academic Alliance) software; often distributed through ELMS (the E-academy License Management System), a system for distributing software packages to academic institutions. NOTE: Secure Download Cabinet files should open automatically with UnpackSDC (unpacksdc.exe) when downloaded. This will extract and install the contents and will delete the SDC file when completed. Therefore, if the SDC file is still on your hard disk after the product has downloaded, you may need to delete the SDC file and try the process again. Windows Microsoft UnpackSDC. Archive of files downloaded with Stardock Central, an enhanced download manager for Stardock software programs; contains installers that have been previously downloaded. Stardock SDC files are created as backup files and are saved in the Program Files/Stardock/Stardock Central/BACKUP directory by default. They can be used to reinstall program updates or to move previous installations to another system. Windows Stardock Central —  (Discontinued). Spreadsheet created with the Calc spreadsheet program included with Apache OpenOffice and StarOffice; includes flexible cell formatting options, such as freely rotating contents, backgrounds, borders, and templates. SDC files can be exported in the Microsoft Excel (.XLS) or Portable Document (.PDF) formats from within Calc. NOTE: Apache OpenOffice was formerly known as OpenOffice.org. Windows OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Calc. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Calc. LibreOfficeFree. An SDC file is a database file used by dictionary applications developed by Paragon Software, most popularly Oxford Advanced Learners Dictionary. It contains dictionary-related content, such as words, definitions, and word pronunciation audio. SDC files are typically large, more than 400MB in size. SDC files are stored on the SD card of an Android device. For example, the SDC file for the Oxford Advanced Learners Dictionary can be found in the following location: /​sdcard/​Android/​data/​com.slovoed.oald/​files/​. Android Oxford Advanced Learners Dictionary.",
    "Windows Microsoft UnpackSDC. Windows Stardock Central —  (Discontinued). Windows OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Calc. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Android Oxford Advanced Learners Dictionary.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".XZ",
    "XZ Compressed Archive",
    "3.5",
    "An XZ file is an archive compressed using XZ compression, a high-ratio compression algorithm based on the LZMA algorithm. It contains one or more files compressed by the xz command-line tool included with XZ Utils. Much like a.ZIP file, an XZ file contains files that have been compressed so they can be stored and shared with others more easily. Users often use XZ files to share compressed files over the Internet, via email, and on USB drives. XZ compression compresses files to smaller sizes than some alternatives, such as gzip and bzip2 compression. For this reason, XZ archives often contain compressed versions of large files, such as Slackware Linux package distributions and.ISO files. NOTE: XZ files that contain a.TAR archive are saved as.TXZ files. You can decompress XZ archives and view their contents with a variety of decompression utilities, including: XZ Utils (Linux) 7-Zip (Windows) WinRAR (Windows) Apple Archive Utility (macOS) The Unarchiver (macOS). Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. 7-Zip. RARLAB WinRAR. ExtractNow. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. Corel WinZip Mac. The Unarchiver. Keka. Zip File Unarchiver. Linux Tukaani XZ Utils. Android RARLAB RAR.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. 7-Zip. RARLAB WinRAR. ExtractNow. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. Corel WinZip Mac. The Unarchiver. Keka. Zip File Unarchiver. Linux Tukaani XZ Utils. Android RARLAB RAR.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".Z",
    "Unix Compressed File",
    "3.5",
    "Compressed file used to store, or pack, files on Unix-based machines; incorporates a simple compression algorithm that is used to archive files and save disk space; can be decompressed on a Unix system by typing uncompress filename.z, where filename.z is the name of the file to decompress. Z files have mostly been replaced by GNUzip compression, which creates.GZ files. Unix users can use the znew utility to recompress Z files to GZ files. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Corel WinZip Mac. Incredible Bee Archiver. The Unarchiver. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Corel WinZip. RARLAB WinRAR. 7-Zip. Linux uncompress Included with OS. gzip. zcat Included with OS. znew Included with OS. unpack Archive Manager Included with OS. Android File Viewer for Android.",
    "Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Corel WinZip Mac. Incredible Bee Archiver. The Unarchiver. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Corel WinZip. RARLAB WinRAR. 7-Zip. Linux uncompress Included with OS. gzip. zcat Included with OS. znew Included with OS. unpack Archive Manager Included with OS. Android File Viewer for Android.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".WASTICKERS",
    "Sticker Maker Sticker Pack",
    "3.5",
    "A WASTICKERS file is a sticker pack created by Viko & Co. Sticker maker, an Android app used to create WhatsApp Messenger stickers. It contains multiple.WEBP stickers, as well as a.PNG icon that represents the sticker pack in WhatsApp. WASTICKERS files also contain.TXT files that list the packs author and title. WASTICKERS file open in Apple Finder Sticker maker allows WhatsApp users to create custom stickers and import those stickers into WhatsApp. After importing their sticker pack, users can add those stickers to WhatsApp messages. Sticker maker allows users to save and share sticker packs as WASTICKER files. WASTICKERS files are compressed with Zip-compression and typically contain at least three stickers. Each sticker is a 512 x 512 pixel WEBP image with a transparent background. Each sticker pack also includes a sticker tray icon, which is a 96 x 96 pixel PNG image. You can open a WASTICKERS file in Viko & Co. Sticker maker (Android). If you dont have access to Sticker maker but want to view the images a WASTICKERS file contains, you can decompress the file as you would any.ZIP file. For example, you can decompress the file using Corel WinZip for Android, 7-Zip (Windows) or Apple Archive Utility (Mac). Before decompressing your WASTICKERS file, you may have to rename it to use the.zip extension. Windows 7-Zip. PeaZip. B1. Archiver. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. B1. Archiver. Linux PeaZip. B1. Archiver. Android Viko & Co. Sticker maker. Corel WinZip for Android. ZDevs ZArchiverFree.",
    "Windows 7-Zip. PeaZip. B1. Archiver. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. B1. Archiver. Linux PeaZip. B1. Archiver. Android Viko & Co. Sticker maker. Corel WinZip for Android. ZDevs ZArchiver.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".PACKAGE",
    "Linux Autopackage File",
    "3.5",
    "A PACKAGE file is a resource package file used by various Electronic Arts (EA) games, including The Sims 2, The Sims 3, The Sims 4, The Sims Online, Spore, SimCity 4, and SimCity (2013). It stores an archive of one or more game files, often in XML format, and may include 3D models, textures, sounds, and other game data, such as characters and neighborhood information. PACKAGE files are saved in EAs standard DBPF archive format. Many PACKAGE files can be edited and repackaged with SimPE, a free editor for The Sims 2. They may also be created and modified with The Sims 2 ContentManager, a program officially released by Electronic Arts for modifying The Sims 2 content. Windows Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. S3PE. Ambertation SimPE. SporeEdit. SporeMaster. SimCityPak. Mac Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts SimCity. Electronic Arts Spore. Archive containing contents of a Linux program and associated files; created with the Autopackage package management system for Linux; installed using the Autopackage installer program. Autopackage is intended for creating application installers rather than system level installers. Linux Autopackage. A PACKAGE file contains an art kit for FOREVER Artisan, a digital scrapbooking application. It stores scrapbooking content, such as page templates, cards, seasonal decorations, and creative splatters, which can be added to scrapbook projects. PACKAGE files are typically purchased and downloaded from the FOREVER online store and imported into the program. Digital art kits may also be saved in an SBKIT or PAKIT file. You can import a kit in Artisan by selecting Import content from the Home menu. NOTE: FOREVER was formerly known as Panstoria and Artisan is based off Storybook Creator, which was formerly known as Panstoria. Windows FOREVER Artisan. A PACKAGE file is an offline update package used by MOBILedit Forensic Express, a program used to extract and analyze mobile device data. It contains data used to update or add a feature to MOBILedit Forensic Express. Users download MOBILedit PACKAGE files from the Downloads section of the programs website. MOBILedit Forensic Express is an application that investigators can use to extract data from mobile devices and mobile device backups. They can then use MOBILedit Forensic Express to analyze the data and generate reports. Periodically, developer Compelson Labs releases updates and add-ons for MOBILedit Forensic Express. These updates are available in the programs online download center. After users log in to the download center, they can download all available updates. Each update is saved as a PACKAGE file. Users can then install their PACKAGE files in MOBILedit Forensic Express. To install a PACKAGE file in MOBILedit Forensic Express (Windows): Open MOBILedit Forensic Express. Select Check for updates. Select Import package. Navigate to and open your PACKAGE file. Windows MOBILedit Forensic Express.",
    "Windows Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts Spore. Electronic Arts SimCity. S3PE. Ambertation SimPE. SporeEdit. SporeMaster. SimCityPak. Mac Electronic Arts The Sims 2. Electronic Arts The Sims 3. Electronic Arts The Sims 4. Electronic Arts SimCity. Electronic Arts Spore. Linux Autopackage. Windows FOREVER Artisan. Windows MOBILedit Forensic Express.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SNB",
    "S Note File",
    "3.5",
    "An SNB file is a note created by S Note, an advanced note-taking application developed by Samsung for use with Samsung mobile devices, such as Galaxy S and Galaxy Note. It contains a note, which may include text, video, audio, sketches, and images. SNB files were replaced by.SPD files. Notes created with S Note can be synced across devices including a PC. SNB files can be exported to.JPG or.PDF files from the S Note app. You can also back up SNB files by syncing them to Google Drive by tapping the the three-line icon in the top right-hand corner, selecting Sync, choosing Google. You can open SNB files in the Samsung Notes app on your Samsung device. In Windows, you can convert SNB files to PDF files on your computer using snbopen. You can also open SNB files in Windows or macOS by replacing the .snb extension with .zip to create a.ZIP file. You can then extract the contents with a Zip decompression program, such as Microsoft File Explorer, Corel WinZip, or Apple Archive Utility. Windows snbopen. Samsung S Note. Android Samsung S Note Included with OS. eBook file created for use with the Bambook, a Chinese e-reader created by Nut Shell Electronics; contains a digital publication similarly to an.EPUB file. The Bambook was originally released in China but is now available in the United States. Nut Shell Electronics is a subsidiary of Shanda Corp. NOTE: SNB files are created exclusively for the Bambook and very few other e-readers are able to read them, but they can be converted into a more accessible format. Windows Calibre. Mac Calibre. Linux CalibreFree.",
    "Windows snbopen. Samsung S Note. Android Samsung S Note Included with OS. Windows Calibre. Mac Calibre. Linux Calibre.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".SDOC",
    "Samsung Notes Note",
    "3.5",
    "An SDOC file is a note created by Samsung Notes, a note-taking app available for Samsung devices. It is a Zip-compressed archive that may contain text, handwritten notes, images, sketches, and audio. SDOC files can be opened with Samsung Notes or decompressed to view their contents. Samsung Notes is a note-taking app installed on some Samsung smartphones, such as the Samsung Galaxy Note and S7, and other devices. Before 2020, when a user saved a note in Samsung Notes, the note was saved as an SDOC file. Contrary to what you might expect, SDOC files are not text files. Instead, they are Zip-compressed archives that contain the text, image, and other files that make up a note. In 2020, Samsung replaced the SDOC format with the.SDOCX format. Now, when users open SDOC files in Samsung Notes, the app automatically converts those files into SDOCX files. Users can also manually convert their SDOC files to SDOCX files using the Old format notes → Convert option available in Samsung Notes settings menu. On Samsung devices, you can open SDOC files with Samsung Notes. You can also use Notes Share function to share your SDOC files with Google Drive, which will allow you to open your notes on other Samsung devices. If you do not have access to Samsung Notes, you can rename your SDOC file to a.ZIP file, decompress it, and view its contents as you would any Zip archive. This will allow you to access the text and media contained within your note and manually reconstruct the note if necessary. If you want to share a note you created in Samsung Notes with someone else or open the note outside Samsung Notes, you can covert the note to a.PDF or.DOCX file. To convert an SDOC note to another file format: Open Samsung Notes and open the note you want to convert to another format. Select the More options (three vertical dots) menu. Then, select Save as file. Select the format in which you want to save your note (such as PDF file or Microsoft Word file). Then, specify what location your file should be saved in and select Save. Windows Samsung Notes. 7-Zip. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. Android Samsung NotesFree. Sealed Word document (.DOC file) created by Oracles IRM document protection software; locks the document so that it can only be viewed by a user with sufficient rights; used for securing the distribution of business documents and email attachments. SDOC files can be viewed using Oracle IRM Desktop, a program that unseals the documents for viewing. However, the documents can only be viewed if the user has the necessary rights. IRM software also sometimes integrates into corporate Word installations and provides an option to seal a document after editing it. NOTE: Oracle IRM software also creates several other sealed file types, such as sealed.PDF files (.SPDF extension). Windows Oracle IRM Desktop. Microsoft Word with IRM add-on. Document created by Satra Khmer, a program used for protecting document text; contains text that has been transposed from regular text to Satra text using the proprietary Transposition System; used for storing sensitive information. NOTE: The Satra Khmer user interface is displayed in the Khmer language, which is also known as Cambodian. The application is no longer available for download. Windows Driver-TC group Satra Khmer.",
    "Windows Samsung Notes. 7-Zip. Mac Apple Archive Utility Included with OS. Android Samsung Notes. Windows Oracle IRM Desktop. Microsoft Word with IRM add-on. Windows Driver-TC group Satra Khmer.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".0",
    "Hacha Split Archive File",
    "3.5",
    "A 0 file is a link file used by Linux operating systems. It contains a reference to a particular version of the library, which may have an extension such as .0.0.0 or .0.0.1, depending on the library version. 0 files allow multiple versions of library files to exist while only one of them is referenced and used by the operating systems dynamic library loader. The library linking convention helps users and the operating system avoid situations where many implementations of the same library interface are loaded at the same time. NOTE: The .0 extension may also refer to an actual shared library and not a link file. Both shared libraries and shared library link files may also use extensions such as .1, .2, and .3. For example, the following are valid extensions:.SO.0, .so.1, .so.2, and .so.3.. Linux Linux dynamic link loader. First part of a split archive created with Hacha, a file archive splitting utility; supports various types of file compression and adds a number the end of each filename; i.e. archive.zip.0, archive.zip.1, archive.zip.2, etc. Hacha is written in the Spanish language (Hacha means Axe in English). Windows Dr. Software Hacha or Hacha Pro. File saved by the M3 DS Real, a multipurpose game cartridge for the Nintendo DS; can store games, movies, and music that can be played on the NDS; automatically created when a game is loaded from the M3 DS Real for the first time; can also be saved manually like a regular game cartridge. Data can be transferred to an M3 DS Real cartridge by connecting the cartridge to a PC via USB and dragging files to it like a hard drive or flash memory device. Windows Transfer to an M3 DS cartridge Not meant to be opened on a PC. Course.0 is an incomplete Mario Kart Wii level file that was mistakenly included in the final version of the game. It contains an uncompressed prototype of the Bowsers Castle course included in Mario Kart Wii. Course.0 is not playable within Mario Kart Wii, as it is not saved in the compressed.KMP format Mario Kart Wii uses to load courses. Intrepid Mario Kart Wii modders found course.0 within the games koopa_course.szs file. This unusual file was saved in a format not used by any of Mario Kart Wiis other files. The modders soon discovered that the file included an early version of the games Bowsers Castle racetrack, which had been created in 2007 and not deleted before Mario Kart Wii shipped in 2008. Modders analyzed course.0 to further their knowledge of how Mario Kart Wii racetracks are developed and created. Some even attempted to convert course.0 into a usable Mario Kart Wii course. Because course.0 is an incomplete Mario Kart Wii course that is not saved in the KMP file format, it cannot be opened or played in Mario Kart Wii. You can, however, open course.0 in a text editor to view the XML data it contains. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor Linux Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. A 0 file is an Android digital certificate. It contains credentials used to verify a website, network, or applications identity and authenticity. You can install 0 files at the user level on any Android device, but you can install 0 files at the system level on only rooted Android devices. Devices, networks, websites, and applications use digital certificates, issued by certificate authorities (CAs), to identify themselves to each other and confirm you are transmitting information between trusted parties. Sometimes, websites, networks, and applications will require you to download and manually install a digital certificate, so you can securely exchange information. On Android, some digital certificates are saved as 0 files (others are saved as.CRT,.P12, or.PFX files). 0 files can be installed at the user level or the system level, which determines whether all Android apps trust the certificate by default. However, to install a 0 file at the system level, you must possess a rooted Android device and manually move the 0 file to your devices system/​etc/​security/​cacerts directory. In most cases, you can simply install 0 files at the user level, and the apps that require that certificate will function correctly. To install a 0 file at the user level on Android: Place the 0 file on your Android devices SD card. Open your devices Settings app and select Security → Encryption & Credentials. Select Install from storage. Select CA Certificate. Click through the warning message Android displays. Navigate to and select your 0 file. Androids certificate manager will open, allowing you to install your certificate. After you install a 0 file, Android will automatically delete the file from its current location and place it in the data/​misc/​user/​0/​cacerts-added directory. Android Google Android Included with OS.",
    "Linux Linux dynamic link loader. Windows Dr. Software Hacha or Hacha Pro. Windows Transfer to an M3 DS cartridge Not meant to be opened on a PC. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Linux Github Atom —  (Discontinued). Any text editor. Android Google Android Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["compressed_files",
    ".S02",
    "ZipSplitter Part 3 File",
    "3.5",
    "An S02 file is the third part of a file that was split using ZipSplitter, a program used to split files to reduce their size for easier portability. It contains a segment of a larger file, such as a.ZIP or.MOV file, that is one part of several other parts. S02 files can be restored by ZipSplitter, along with the other parts (.S00,.S01, etc.) by double-clicking the.EXE file included with the split archive. Windows Lithops Software ZipSplitter.",
    "Windows Lithops Software ZipSplitter.",
    "?"],
