    "Gzipped Javascript File",
    "3.3",
    "Javascript (.JS) file zipped using GZip (.GZ) compression; typically used for shrinking the file sizes of large Javascript documents referenced by websites; can be decompressed on the fly by most Web servers using a Gzip utility. JGZ files are also used by the JNode operating system. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Corel WinZip. RARLAB WinRAR. 7-Zip. Linux gzipFree.",
